-## 8. Monitoring & Metrics
+## 8. Rate Limiting Configuration
+
+The gateway applies per-client-IP rate limits before routing requests. Configure
+rate limiting in `config/gateway.conf` with global defaults plus optional
+version-specific overrides:
+
+```conf
+rate_limit_enabled = true
+rate_limit_requests = 100
+rate_limit_window_seconds = 60
+rate_limit_v1 = 60:60
+rate_limit_v2 = 500:60
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true`/`false` | Enables or disables rate limiting globally. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Default number of requests allowed from one client IP during the window. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Default rate-limit window length in seconds. |
+| `rate_limit_<version>` | `requests:seconds` | Override for a specific API version, such as `rate_limit_v1 = 60:60`. |
+
+Version-specific limits are isolated from one another: exhausting the `v1` quota
+does not consume quota for the same client on `v2`. If no version-specific limit
+exists, the gateway falls back to the global default of `100` requests per `60`
+seconds.
+
+When the limit is exceeded, the gateway returns HTTP `429` with a JSON error
+response.
+
+---
